ty","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210114190","name":"Shanghai Zhangjiang Laboratory","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210116208","name":"Linkou Chang Gung Memorial Hospital","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210120917","name":"Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company (Taiwan)","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210121532","name":"Ministry of Health and Welfare","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210126829","name":"China Medical University Hospital","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210131804","name":"National Taiwan University Hospital","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210135784","name":"Institute of Atomic and Molecular Sciences, Academia Sinica","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210136969","name":"Institute of Molecular Biology, Academia Sinica","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"US","id":"I4210137306","name":"Stanford Medicine","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210142271","name":"Wan Fang Hospital","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4210158385","name":"Taipei Medical University-Shuang Ho Hospital","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4405256935","name":"Zhangjiang Laboratory","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4405280835","name":"Zhanjiang University of Science and Technology","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"JP","id":"I4405285965","name":"Nagoya University Future Earth Research Center","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I47519274","name":"Taipei Medical University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I4880106","name":"Feng Chia University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"JP","id":"I73613424","name":"National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"US","id":"I74973139","name":"Carnegie Mellon University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"US","id":"I78577930","name":"Columbia University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I79223203","name":"Guangdong Ocean University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I84653119","name":"Academia Sinica","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I87354575","name":"National Chengchi University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I882009436","name":"Central Taiwan University of Science and Technology","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I91807558","name":"National Cheng Kung University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I96852419","name":"Capital Normal University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"US","id":"I97018004","name":"Stanford University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I99613584","name":"National Taipei University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"TW","id":"I99908691","name":"Yuan Ze University","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":null,"rising_score":null,"work_count":1,"work_ids":["W7163038666"]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"Abstract Nano- and microplastics (NMPs), by-products of the fragmentation and degradation of plastic products, are ubiquitous environmental contaminants, yet their burden in pediatric immune tissues and functional consequences for developing immunity remain unknown. Here we report the first comprehensive characterization of NMPs in surgically excised pediatric tonsils (n = 30) using pyrolysis gas chromatography\u2013 mass spectrometry (Py-GC/MS), Nile Red fluorescence microscopy, and optical photothermal infrared (O-PTIR) spectroscopy. NMPs were detected in all specimens, with polystyrene, polyethylene, polyethylene terephthalate, and acrylonitrile butadiene styrene present in >90% of samples. To bridge clinical exposure data with mechanistic insight, we formulated a cryo-milled multi-polymer mixture reflecting the patient-derived polymer profile and challenged human lymphoid aggregate culture (HLAC) tonsil organoids at environmentally relevant concentrations. Multiplexed cytokine profiling of culture supernatants revealed a robust early inflammatory response at day 3, with significant upregulation of IL-6 (p = 0.011) and MIP-1\u03b2/CCL4 (p = 0.011), followed by convergence toward control levels by day 14. Functional cytokine modules spanning immune, metabolic, structural, and growth factor pathways showed coordinated deviation from controls at day 3 post-exposure with subsequent normalization. Fluorescence-guided depth profiling demonstrated time-dependent penetration of 100 nm particles into organoid aggregates (70% tissue depth at day 3 versus 95% at day 14), and transmission electron microscopy revealed intracellular polyethylene within lymphocyte lysosomes. These findings establish pediatric tonsils as a sentinel tissue for NMP bioaccumulation and demonstrate that environmentally relevant polymer mixtures elicit transient but significant immunomodulatory responses in human lymphoid tissue, with implications for mucosal and systemic immune health in children. Abstract Figure Structure: Translational pipeline from clinical tissue characterization to patient-informed preclinical modeling of nano-microplastic (NMP) exposure in pediatric lymphoid tissue. Pediatric tonsil tissue collected from clinically indicated tonsillectomies underwent tissue digestion for NMP characterization to identify NMP type and size distributions. In parallel, tonsil tissue was used to generate human lymphoid aggregate culture (HLAC) organoids that recapitulate the cellular complexity of the native tissue. These patient-derived organoids were then exposed to environmentally relevant compositions and concentrations of NMPs over time-course experiments, with longitudinal assessment of immunomodulatory responses including cytokine profiling and functional readouts. This bedside-to-bench approach establishes a physiologically relevant human system for investigating NMP-immune interactions, bridging clinical tissue analysis with mechanistic preclinical modeling to inform understanding of pediatric environmental exposures and their potential health impacts.","author_count":15,"author_ids":["A5015595722","A5022444518","A5034270149","A5039497136","A5042231568","A5083437044","A5087595212","A5092974728","A5111690381","A5126703410","A5135072795","A5135092863","A5137430624","A5137559060","A5137588000"],"author_institution_ids":["I16733864","I4210137306","I97018004"],"authors":[{"id":"A5034270149","name":"Amirbahador Golchin"},{"id":"A5126703410","name":"Antony Georgiadis"},{"id":"A5137588000","name":"Maggie H Zhang"},{"id":"A5083437044","name":"Yi\u2010Cheng Lin"},{"id":"A5092974728","name":"Isha Kandlikar"},{"id":"A5022444518","name":"Patrick Timothy Kiessling"},{"id":"A5087595212","name":"Mitra A. Alikhani"},{"id":"A5137430624","name":"Andrea Miranda"},{"id":"A5039497136","name":"Nathan J. Alves"},{"id":"A5135072795","name":"Alex Bindemann"},{"id":"A5135092863","name":"Anushri Umesh"},{"id":"A5042231568","name":"Matthew J. Campen"},{"id":"A5111690381","name":"Robert Taylor"},{"id":"A5137559060","name":"Stacey Harper"},{"id":"A5015595722","name":"Kara D. Meister"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":0,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.05.27.728317","domain_tags":["analytical_methods","fate_transport_and_sorption"],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I131249849","I157725225","I16733864","I169521973","I219193219","I4210137306","I4394709130","I97018004"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"bioRxiv (Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory)","last_updated":"2026-11-09T13:22:03.289127","license":"cc-by-nd","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"green","oa_url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2026/06/01/2026.05.27.728317.full.pdf","openalex_topics":["T10419","T10753","T14072"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2026-06-01","study_type":"preprint","title":"Nano- and microplastics in pediatric tonsil tissue: bioaccumulation, distribution, and immunomodulatory effects in human lymphoid aggregate organoids","type":"preprint","work_id":"W7163038666","year":2026}]}
